WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.990
Bend a thin rod into a ring, and
spread charge evenly around it.

2
00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:09.120
At the very middle of the ring,
the field is exactly zero.

3
00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:12.900
Step a little way along the
axis, out of the ring's plane.

4
00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.780
Now there is a field.

5
00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.470
Go far away, and the ring
acts like a point charge.

6
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:22.550
So why is the field zero at the
middle, but not just off it?

7
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:26.400
In this mission, you'll slice
charged objects into tiny pieces,

8
00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.290
and add up their fields.

9
00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.730
Then you'll find the
fields of a charged rod,

10
00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.890
an arc, and an infinitely long line.

11
00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:38.430
Your mission: explain why the field
appears once you step off the middle.
